Subject: CK: store the exact per-row max logit next to the FMHA forward LSE

Add fmha_fwd_args::max_ptr (fp32, same layout and strides as lse_ptr) for
the max logit used by QK-clip / MuonClip: the max of the softmax inputs over
the unmasked keys, -inf for fully masked rows.

The qr, qr_async and qr_async_trload forward pipelines keep an exact running
row max (kStoreRowMax), updated before the conditional rescale that can leave
m up to 8 log2 units below it, and store it next to the LSE in the same
units. The store is gated at runtime on max_ptr, so no kernel instances are
added. Only instances that store the LSE and have no bias, dropout or sink
carry it: in the others the extra live tile costs occupancy or spills (up to
14% on the d64 group-mode sink kernel) whether or not the max is requested.
Those instances, with max_ptr in its own kargs mixin, compile to the same
code as before. fmha_fwd_create_kargs_and_grids throws when max_ptr is set
for an instance without kStoreRowMax, or together with sink_ptr.

Masked qr_async row-max instances with 32 < d <= 64 ask for four blocks per
CU, which the extra register would otherwise drop to three.

